  "package": "flag",
  "notes": "flag: Go's grammar, error texts and PrintDefaults layout on FlagSet and the command-line set. Flag variables are shared Ptr<T> handles instead of *T. Rust substitutions for reflection: Value has provided is_bool_flag/kind/zero_string/as_getter methods (a custom value without zero_string counts as zero when its default text is empty; a panicking String on a zero value is not caught), usage callbacks take &FlagSet (the package-level readers work from inside the command-line usage on a snapshot; modifying the set there panics), Set records the caller through #[track_caller].",
