    "FlagSet.PrintDefaults": {
      "rust": "rust_stdlib::flag::FlagSet::print_defaults",
      "deviation": "reflection+panic-hook-output",
      "note": "Go decides whether a default is the zero value by reflecting a fresh zero of the Value's type and calling String on it. Built-in values answer through Value::zero_string; for a custom Value without it the default counts as zero when its text is empty. A panic in that call is caught and reported after the listing as Go does (panic calling String method on zero <type> for flag <name>: <message>); the type is Value::type_name, a Rust path instead of Go's package.Type. A panic from a zero value's String is recovered and reported as Go does, but Rust's panic hook still prints to stderr where Go's recover is silent."
    },
