      "note": "While the command-line set's usage message runs, the package-level readers (PrintDefaults, NFlag, Arg(s), Parsed, Lookup, Visit, VisitAll) work on a frozen snapshot, so the usual Usage = func(){ ...; flag.PrintDefaults() } works. Defining, setting or parsing flags from inside the callback is not possible (the set is exclusively borrowed by the running parse, and Rust forbids the aliasing); such calls panic with a message instead of deadlocking.",
